I'm extremely loath to tell people to write code like this <@!425572898787426305> <@!291925846556540928>:
```typescript
try {
    eth_getBlockByNumber('finalized')
    // TODO: PoS finalized-based decision making
} catch (error) {
    if (error.message === NO_FINALIZED_BLOCK_YET_MESSAGE) {
        // TODO: PoW confirmation-based decision making
    }
}
```
There are books (probably) written on why this is ~~bad~~ terrible code.

If your basis on this being terrible is the try/catch I don't see why that's needed:

```
response = eth_getBlockByNumber('finalized')
if response.error && response.error.message == NO_FINALIZED_BLOCK_YET_MESSAGE { 
   // POW
} else {
   // POS
}
```

But maybe you meant having to check the blockbynumber result at all?
